          %h3#the_prequantum_geometry The prequantum geometry
          %p
            We first discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
            on the 2-sphere
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#PrequantumBundleWithoutConnection"} Without connection
          %p
            and then consider genuine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundles"} prequantum line bundles
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#PrequantumConnection"} With connection
              \.
          %h4#PrequantumBundleWithoutConnection Prequantum bundle without connection
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Hermitian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
              are classified via their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
              (just as
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
              a line bundle given by two trivializing sections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_\pm
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mo ±
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{\pm}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              has class the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/winding+number"} winding number
              of the transition function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mn 2
                        %msubsup
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^1 \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C} - \{0\}
                    \\stackrel{s_2 s_1^{-1}}{\to} \mathbb{C}^\times
                    \\,.
          #StandardCechCocycle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{Z} \simeq H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z})
              we take the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycle
              representing this class to be that given on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo −
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_+ \cap U_- \simeq S^2 - \{x_0, x_\infty\}
              by the transition function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msubsup
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi z
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f(z_+) \coloneqq z_+^{-k} = z_-^{k}
                    \\,.
          #SpinStructureByThetaCharacteristic.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              By the discussion there, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
              is equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Line
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{\Omega^{1,0}} \in \mathbf{Line}_{\mathbb{C}}(S^2)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+line+bundle"} canonical line bundle
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{1,0}
          #CanonicalBundleAndSquareRoot.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+line+bundle"} canonical line bundle
              on the 2-sphere is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c_1\left(\Omega^{1,0}\left(S^2\right)\right)
                    \=
                    2
                    \\in
                    \\mathbb{Z} \simeq H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z})
            %p
              (up to a unique choice of sign, which determines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              on the right). Accordingly the 2-sphere has an essentially unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+characteristic"} theta characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{\Omega^{1,0}}
              is the complex line bundle with unit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msqrt
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mrow
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 0
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                            %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c_1\left(\sqrt{\Omega^{1,0}\left(S^2\right)}\right)
                    \=
                    1
                    \\in
                    \\mathbb{Z} \simeq H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z})
                    \\,,
            %p
              the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basic+line+bundle+on+the+2-sphere"} basic line bundle on the 2-sphere
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The canonical section of the holomorphic 1-form bundle on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              is simply the canonical 1-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d z
              itself. By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+charts"} coordinate charts
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RiemannSphere"}
              we have on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C} - \{0\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mo −
                    %mo =
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msubsup
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d z_- = d (z_+^{-1}) = - z_+^{-2} d z_+
            %p and so the transition function of the canonical bundle in this local trivialization is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \- z^{-2} \colon (\mathbb{C}-\{0\}) \to \mathbb{C}^\times
            %p
              as in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardCechCocycle"}
            %p
              This has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/winding+number"} winding number
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
              of the holomorphic 1-form bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{1,0}
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ±
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1(\Omega^{1,0}) =  \pm 2
              (the sign being an arbitrary convention, determined by the identification
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              And so it follows that there is a unique spin structure, namely given by choosing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{\Omega^{1,0}}
              to be the line bundle on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
              with first Chern class
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ±
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1
          %h4#PrequantumConnection Prequantum bundle with connection
          %p
            We discuss equipping the above complex line bundles on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
          #DeligneCocycle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in  H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycle
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardCechCocycle"}
              to a Cech-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cocycle
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+form"} Kähler form
              of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KaehlerStructure"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∂
                    %mover
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega = \partial \overline{\partial} K
            %p
              by taking the connection 1-form on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo ±
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{\pm}
              to be
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi θ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mi exp
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi K
                              %mo )
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi exp
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi K
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi K
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi k
                            %mfrac
                              %mover
                                %mi z
                                %mo ¯
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mi z
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %mn 2
                            %mi d
                            %mi z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\theta
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\exp\left(-K\right)
                    {\partial}
                    \\exp\left(K\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    {\partial} K
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = k \frac{\overline{z} }{ 1 + {\vert z\vert}^2} d {z}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          #DeligneCocycleIsConsistent.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The Cech-Deligne cocycle in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeligneCocycle"}
              is indeed well defined.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We need to check that the connection 1-form satisfies on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo −
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_+ \cap U_- \simeq (S^2 - \{x_0, x_\infty\})
              the transition law
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi k
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mo −
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta_+ \;+\; z^{-k} d z^k \;=\; \theta_-
                    \\,.
            %p
              To see this first notice that on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mo −
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_+ \cap U_- \simeq (\mathbb{C} - \{0\})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
